WEBVTT

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.580
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.080
You really are no different from an animal!

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.000
Even your cries before dying are ignoble!

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.910
S-Stop...!

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.000
<i>The mist is hiding the sin</i>

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.750
<i>I hold in my hand the LIST of judgment</i>

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.370
<i>I'm gonna do the perfect crime</i>
<i>and bury them in a cist</i>

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:11.620
<i>That's my DYING WISH for you</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:17.080
<i>Guys of the privileged class torment the weak</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.160
<i>And they enjoy it</i>

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.700
<i>That's a bloody world, an endlessly</i>
<i>discriminatory society (dystopia)</i>

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.700
<i>Happiness does not bloom here</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.830
<i>We are oppressed</i>

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:39.410
<i>We must do something. Come on</i>

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:45.870
<i>Let the end begin</i>

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:51.700
<i>Break it to relieve your soul</i>

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:57.660
<i>Open your eyes. You'll be reborn</i>
<i>when you lose your life</i>

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:02.750
<i>We're lords of crime. We're sacrifice for ideals</i>

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:15.000
<i>Freedom lives forever, even if we die</i>

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:27.040
What a fine evening this has become.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.870
"The 'Noahtic' Act 2"

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.870
There really is a different zest that goes
with killing with your own hands

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.580
"The 'Noahtic' Act 2"

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.580
as compared to hunting with a gun.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.870
as compared to hunting with a gun.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.750
Perhaps I'll try that sometime
on my hunting ground.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.790
Lord Enders?

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.830
It's Moriarty. Are you all right?

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.580
Moriarty?!

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.660
Th-This is bad! Not right now!

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:53.500
If he finds out I hunted him...!

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.000
I'm letting myself in.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.500
Lord Enders, where are you?

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.790
J-Just a moment!

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.330
Oh, my...

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:11.910
Whatever do we have here?

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.370
I don't suppose <i>you</i>...

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.950
No! Just a moment! It's not like that!

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:20.830
H-He attacked me with a knife,
and out of nowhere, I, uh...

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.500
You mean he is a thief?

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.160
Yeah! That's right! A robber!

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.330
This despicable commoner
was lurking in my stateroom!

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:34.700
However, for him being a thief, I don't see
any signs of your room being ransacked.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:39.620
Moreover, this was a thrust through
the heart, with no hesitation.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:44.450
From what I can see, the handle of
the weapon is fairly exquisitely made.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.540
It does not at all appear to be something
a commoner would carry.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.330
It must belong to you.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:56.000
D-Do you doubt my word?!

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.540
No.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.750
You are a proud nobleman.
I believe what you say.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:06.620
Besides which, there is no way you
would do something as unmerited

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:10.040
as killing a commoner for no reason.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.330
Qu-Quite right!

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:16.830
However, circumstantially, it will be
difficult to prove to a third party

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:20.040
that this man was a thief.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:24.370
Has anyone other than myself
seen what happened here?

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:25.950
No.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.080
Then that simplifies matters.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.950
What if we were to discard him
into the sea, right away?

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:35.250
We are at sea on a moonless night.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.830
There is no situation more favourable than this

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:41.290
for disposing of a rotten apple
without anyone knowing.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.950
Are you ready?

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.250
Yeah.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.120
--Heave, ho!
--Heave, ho!

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.500
Whoops! Pardon me.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.790
No, that's all right.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.120
Well, we should be getting back.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.790
No one has noticed a thing.
There is naught to worry about.

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.250
Still...

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:11.700
Even if some soul were to realise
he has disappeared from the ship,

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.620
they will likely conclude that he
became inebriated and fell into the sea.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:19.790
It happens quite often on
ocean voyages, after all.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.580
You're right...

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:27.160
Yeah, mm-hmm, you're right!

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.410
I suspect it goes without saying,
but this whole affair...

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.620
Our little secret, of course.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.250
I owe you for this, Moriarty!

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:53.080
I must say, I can hardly wait!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.870
The ballet performance is tonight.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.160
Is it not much too early
for you to grow so restive?

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.290
As it happens, Lord Enders has gone through
the trouble of saving a choice seat for me.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.330
That is why I am so jovial.

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:09.950
Ha! Is that why?

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.580
No wonder you are looking forward to it.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.330
Bravo!

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:41.450
Bravo! Oh, that was wonderful!
It was worth coming for this.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.330
Indeed it was.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:47.620
That was the end of the first act.
Very well, I will be excusing myself now.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:50.500
Oh, are you not staying to watch until the end?

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:55.250
Well, I have a seat saved for me
down on the front row for the second act.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:59.790
That's madness! You're going to watch
from down amongst the commoners?

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:03.870
Ah, whilst it may be a tad uncomfortable
to be surrounded by commoners,

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.160
I thought I might get a closer view.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.250
Oh, I see.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.040
Still, you'd do well to be mindful.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:15.450
I had the most unpleasant experience
with one of them last night.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:20.080
Well, we cannot have that.
I shall take your advice to heart.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.660
I will see you later.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:29.450
Quite the curious turn of events.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:34.620
Lord Enders, might I have a moment?

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.910
Oh, Moriarty!

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:42.370
What's wrong? The look on
your face is positively grim.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:46.660
Actually, it's a matter of no small concern.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:50.000
Lord Enders, are you positive...

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.830
...that you thoroughly killed that man?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.660
What?

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.120
I do hope that I'm mistaken--

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.830
Hold on! What are you saying?!

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.910
Didn't the two of us make sure
to get rid of the body?

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:06.080
Yes... that we did, but here...

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:13.200
Please have a look. Down in the stalls,
forward and on the left.

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:17.290
What exactly am I looking at?

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:19.750
A bit more left.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:24.200
The fourth row from the front,
three seats from the end.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.120
Do you see him?

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:31.000
But that's--!

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.790
Yes. The thief from last night, isn't it?

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:39.120
Impossible! It can't be him!
I killed him with my own two hands!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.000
Assuming, as difficult as it is
to believe, that he is still alive,

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.450
I rushed here to inform you, as well.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:49.330
I see. Thank you, Moriarty.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:51.790
Forgive me, but I must leave!

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:56.830
Off you go... to the second act.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.700
This is bad! So bad! This is very bad!

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.500
This is bad, this is bad,
this is bad, this is bad!

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:08.450
What in God's name is going on?!
Don't tell me he swam back on board!

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:13.660
No, that's impossible! I know I killed him!
I've killed people any number of times!

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:15.620
There can be no doubt!

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.330
He's gone?!

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:23.000
You! What happened to the man
who was sitting there?!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.120
Does anyone know who he is?! I'll pay you money!

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:31.330
Um, that man just left through that doorway.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:37.160
Damn it, damn it, damn it!
How is this happening?!

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:39.620
If he tells anyone about
what happened last night,

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:42.790
it will come out that I tried to kill him!

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:44.950
That would be a disaster!

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:05.370
Currently leading target
along the planned course.

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:20.580
I'm certain... he had to have come down here.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:24.200
But where exactly am I...?

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.790
You surely have put me
through a great deal of bother.

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:40.870
You're dead?

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.660
Why, you--!

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.580
What is this?!

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.750
You really are dead after all!

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:49.660
You rotten scum! You miserable--!

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:53.620
I <i>know</i>... I <i>know </i>I killed him last night.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:56.750
So how did he come back to life?!

00:10:56.750 --> 00:11:04.750
And why is he now dead again?!
Wait, is he dead for sure this time?

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:07.950
I can't have him actually being alive.

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:13.290
I'll have to kill him so dead,
he can never come back to life again!

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:21.500
He's in place. Everything is ready.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.500
Go ahead and raise him up.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:24.910
Understood.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:35.200
Die!

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:38.790
Die! Die! Die for good!

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:44.080
You scum! Don't ever... come back to life again!

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:47.250
You rotten... You rotten...

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:11.120
He killed him!

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:15.790
No, this isn't like that.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.290
He stabbed that man! He killed him!

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.540
This isn't part of the show! It's murder!

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.000
How dreadful!

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.330
You mean, he killed him
right there on the stage?

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:28.000
Oh, is that not...

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.620
...Count Blitz Enders?!

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:34.290
Count Enders?

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:36.120
He's an aristocrat?

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:38.700
How could he do such a thing?

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:41.250
Then the stories about him are true.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.450
About how he hunts people
on his hunting grounds?

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:46.790
How awful! He's a murderer!

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:49.790
What do you take human life for?!

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:01.160
Human life, you say?

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.330
Don't make me laugh.

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:07.330
What's so wrong about killing
the likes of this commoner? Eh?

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:10.160
I am a nobleman!

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:14.500
This is Noah's Ark!

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:18.250
Other than the noblemen on board,
everyone on here is livestock!

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:22.370
Whether I let them live or kill them
is entirely in my hands!

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:26.370
H-Have you gone mad, Enders?!

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:29.450
No matter what you call it,
what you've just done is commit murder!

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:36.160
Wh-Why, you duplicitous cad!
You look down on commoners all the time!

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:40.250
D-Don't you equate me with yourself,
you cold-blooded killer!

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:44.250
Wh-Why, you--!

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:56.750
Now!

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:58.160
Apprehend that man!

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.660
Don't let him escape!

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:03.080
Seize him!

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.290
Huh?

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.450
Well, <i>that's </i>interesting.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.700
Ah, there he is!

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:10.000
Well? No one can come after me up here!

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:14.160
For the rest of your lives, all you can
ever do is keep looking up to me!

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:18.870
I truly am chosen amongst men, the same as Noah!

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:51.120
Moriarty...?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.830
Mr Moran, welcome back.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.750
Yeah. I need whisky.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.790
It's ready for you, right there.

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:33.750
What was the sentiment in town?

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:36.290
The whole place is in a terrible fuss.

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:40.910
A case of murder on the stage of
the maiden voyage of a luxury liner--

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:44.080
it would be far more unreasonable
to expect folk to not be talking about it.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:49.290
It gets better. Rumours are going around
that the man hunted people.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:52.620
There are some MPs in the House of Commons

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:57.000
who are calling for an investigation
of his hunting grounds to verify that.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:00.410
When the day comes that the
investigation is carried out,

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.330
and the bones of those hunted
by Lord Enders are unearthed,

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:07.450
the commonalty are sure to be appalled.

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:11.870
Judging by your expression, you must
have already taken a few measures.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:16.120
Brother is exercising his influence,
which will likely turn out favourably.

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:19.160
Still, this one was a large-scale operation,

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:21.700
so tidying up afterward
has been quite an ordeal.

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.660
Right, Fred?

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:28.290
Tch, as personable as ever.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:33.830
Then again, that was impressive.
I'm surprised it went as smoothly as it did.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:37.410
You must have seen the final painting
from the very beginning.

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:42.200
Yes. With everyone's help,
the plan went off without a hitch.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.250
However...

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:47.790
...one cause for trepidation may have arisen.

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:53.620
There is still no way to ascertain
the degree of threat he poses.

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:57.370
Which is why I must make some
inquiries concerning <i>him</i>.

00:17:57.370 --> 00:18:03.540
Talk to us. If this bloke ends up our foe,
we need to know ahead of time.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:07.790
That being said, all we did
was stand around chatting.

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:10.830
It was as we were disembarking the <i>Noahtic</i>...

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.370
Yo, mathematician!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.450
I've been looking for you.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:32.500
I need someone I can talk to about that
show that was put on aboard the ship.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.450
That was quite the spectacle, wasn't it?

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:37.450
However, I am not all that
knowledgeable about ballet--

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.870
That's not what I meant.

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:43.750
I'm talking about the dramatic murder
in full view of everyone.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:49.580
That was no ordinary killing.

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:51.870
Are you saying that something
about it was contrived?

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:56.700
Yeah, the body. The poor fellow
died the night before.

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.500
From his jaw, to his limbs,

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:02.160
post-mortem rigidity had set in
right down to his fingertips.

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.870
Which means he'd been dead
for 10-15 hours already.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:10.040
No matter how you look at it,
he was not killed up on that stage.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:13.000
So you have knowledge of
forensic pathology, as well?

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:18.250
It's common knowledge around France.
This country is behind the times.

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:23.250
Anyhow, back to the point.
This makes matters highly irregular.

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:25.160
What those in the audience witnessed

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:29.080
was the count in the act of thrusting
his dagger into the victim's body--

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:31.450
the very moment of murder.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:35.000
But afterwards, the count said this...

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:38.370
Don't make me laugh.

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:41.790
What's so wrong about killing
the likes of this commoner?

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:46.660
Which is to say, he was conscious
that he had killed his victim.

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:51.330
However, that was a corpse
that had died the previous night.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.540
Odd, isn't it?

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.540
Yes, indeed so.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:20:01.700
It follows, then, that the count was unaware
of the fact that the victim was already dead.

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:05.870
Which means that he was led to
believe that the corpse was alive.

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:07.870
So it stands to reason...

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:11.790
...that there was likely a third
party that led him to this.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:13.500
A third party?

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:18.700
Yeah. I know it's a wild story, but there's
only one explanation that makes sense.

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:23.660
That being... this whole ship
was the stage for the incident.

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.540
The possibility that through
numerous stratagems,

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:32.910
someone compelled the count to act as he did--
someone who set up that entire scene.

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:37.870
So something on so a grand a scale as this
transpired during the voyage, then?

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:39.790
To what end, exactly?

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:43.160
Ah, not even I could tell you that.

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:47.700
I'm merely stating that if it were
the case, it would all make sense.

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:51.660
I did some digging around the ship
before I got off, just to be sure,

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:55.250
but I didn't find a single thing
that served as proof.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:21:02.000
You went to all that trouble? You must have
been quite sure of your hypothesis.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:03.660
Of course I was.

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:06.660
When you eliminate every other possibility,

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:11.950
then whatever remains, however
improbable, must be the truth.

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:18.410
You are enjoying yourself to no end.

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:24.160
Well, sure I am! I haven't the foggiest
notion who did this, or why,

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:27.830
but they've provided me
with an exquisite mystery!

00:21:27.830 --> 00:21:31.950
A mathematician like yourself
must comprehend my delight, right?

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:35.500
It's in solving mathematical
expressions that the fun lies.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.910
Well, what can I say?

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:43.700
This has been a truly intriguing conversation.

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:46.330
If you'll pardon me, though, I must be leaving.

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:48.410
Sure. See you around.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:52.660
Come to think of it...

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:56.120
...I have yet to ask your name.

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:59.660
My name is Holmes.

00:22:03.410 --> 00:22:06.000
Sherlock Holmes.

00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:11.200
<i>An oath committed by souls assumed,</i>

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:15.410
<i>with ideals that wallow in genetic karma</i>

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:34.500
<i>Lie! Be resolute if you're going</i>
<i>to share your pain</i>

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:36.750
<i>(Demonstrate your resolve)</i>

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:40.250
<i>Like, dislike, you can't afford</i>
<i>to care either way</i>

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:43.450
<i>It depends on the objective</i>
<i>(Making it happen is what's most important)</i>

00:22:43.450 --> 00:22:47.000
<i>The necessary evil of self-sacrifice</i>

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:50.620
<i>is a righteous cause that no one can comprehend</i>

00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:54.370
<i>Take pride in the inviolable bonds shared</i>

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:59.200
<i>among brothers who bear the same crime</i>

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:02.870
<i>Make a chance trigger your inevitable stance</i>

00:23:02.870 --> 00:23:04.540
<i>and get drunk on your accomplishments</i>

00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:06.330
<i>at the end</i>

00:23:06.330 --> 00:23:09.500
<i>Don't believe in what you can see,</i>

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:13.750
<i>in truths there's no point in knowing</i>
<i>(Whatever it takes)</i>

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:20.330
<i>Defer to its own validity,</i>
<i>you only have one goal</i>

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:21.830
<i>(Let me hear you say)</i>

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:28.660
<i>You can't lie to yourself, come along with me</i>

00:23:31.620 --> 00:23:34.330
<i>It's all because there is no answer</i>

00:23:34.330 --> 00:23:36.700
<i>There is no turning back</i>

00:23:45.370 --> 00:23:52.000
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
'A Study in "S" Act 1.'
